+## Setup
+
+Install Node.js 24 (the version range declared in package.json). The tool has no
+package dependencies, so no dependency installation is needed for these commands.
+Run commands from the repository root.
+
+## Usage
+
+Preview the synthetic records shipped with the project:
+
+```sh
+npm run preview -- test/parcels.ndjson
+# Or, without npm's script banner:
+node src/cli.mjs test/parcels.ndjson
+```
+
+The sample contains `demo-101` with status `ready` and `demo-102` with status
+`dispatched`. The command emits this one JSON record:
+
+```json
+{"parcelId":"demo-101","action":"dispatch"}
+```
+
+Provide one JSON object per nonblank input line. Only status `ready` is selected;
+each ready parcel needs a nonempty string `id`. Other statuses are skipped.
+A missing filename prints usage and exits 2; unreadable files, malformed JSON
+and invalid ready IDs raise errors. This is a preview, not a durable queue:
+repeating the same input repeats the same output. Use synthetic examples;
+customer addresses must stay private under the employer policy.
+
+## Development
+
+```sh
+npm test
+```
+
+The two tests cover filtering ready parcels and rejecting a missing identifier.
+See [source responsibilities](src/README.md) for the CLI/data transformation
+boundary. Review production changes with the warehouse-platform owner; the
+release manager schedules carrier integration changes.
